Lens\n**Lens 1: The Intent vs. Reality Check** - Logic Gaps and Inconsistent 
Validation\n\n## Expected vs. Observed\n| Expected Behavior | Observed Risk 
|\n|---|---|\n| Both `_parse_line_ranges` and `_validate_lines_read` should 
treat whitespace-only strings consistently (either both accept as valid "no 
lines read" or both reject as invalid). | `WorkingMemoryEntry` created via 
`from_dict()` (deserialization) with whitespace-only `lines_read` will pass 
validation (because `__post_init__` calls `_validate_lines_read` which raises 
`ValueError`), but `_parse_line_ranges` used in `should_read_file` will return 
empty list, treating it as "no lines read". This creates a validation bypass and
inconsistent state. |\n\n## Root Cause\n1. `_parse_line_ranges` (line 456-457): 
