```\n   - For whitespace-only string `"   "`: `normalized = ""`\n   - `if not 
normalized:` is `True`\n   - Raises `ValueError`\n\n3. 
`WorkingMemoryEntry.__post_init__` calls `_validate_lines_read`\n   - Direct 
creation: `WorkingMemoryEntry(path, purpose, "   ")` raises `ValueError`\n   - 
Deserialization: `WorkingMemoryEntry.from_dict(data)` calls `__post_init__`, 
raises `ValueError`\n\n## Fix Plan\nMake the validation consistent. Since empty 
string `""` is explicitly allowed (means "no lines read"), whitespace-only 
strings should probably also be treated as "no lines read" rather than invalid. 
